Package: svid
Type: Package
Title: Systematic Spectral Index Discovery, Deduplication and Validation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0000-0000-0000")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut"))
Description: A reproducible workflow for discovering spectral indices from
    multispectral and hyperspectral data. Candidate index expressions are
    generated from a configurable grammar over standard band symbols, reduced
    to a non-redundant set by exact symbolic canonicalisation and by detection
    of monotone-equivalent formulations, screened with fast class-separability
    statistics, and evaluated under spatially aware resampling with confidence
    intervals, paired significance tests and mandatory reference baselines.
    Deduplication before ranking is essential: exhaustively generated pools
    typically contain two to three times more expressions than distinguishable
    features, and algebraically identical formulations can receive different
    accuracies. Supports classification and regression, guided search as an
    alternative to enumeration, perturbation and cross-sensor robustness
    testing, radiative-transfer-based screening, raster prediction and
    publication-quality graphics.
